3. Between Monday, October 16, 1995 and Tuesday, December 12, 1995 (both dates inclusive), count of business days. Start: Monday Oct 16; end: Tuesday Dec 12. Compute days. Oct 16: Oct start 274, Oct 16 = 274+15=289. Dec 12: Dec start 335, Dec 12 = 335+11=346. Inclusive days = 346-289+1=58 days. Check: from Oct 16 to Dec 12. Oct has 31 days, so Oct 16-31 = 16 days (16 to 31 inclusive = 16? Actually 31-16+1=16), Nov has 30 days, Dec 1-12 = 12 days, total =16+30+12=58, good. Now day-of-week: Oct 16: day 289, (289-1)=288 mod7= 288/7=41*7=287, remainder1 => Monday? Since Sunday=0, Monday=1, yes Monday. Dec 12: day 346, (346-1)=345 mod7= 7*49=343, remainder2 => Tuesday? Actually 345-343=2, so Tuesday (since 0 Sun,1 Mon,2 Tue). So start Mon, end Tue. Total 58 days. We need Mon-Fri count. We can compute number of weekends. Let's compute number of Saturdays and Sundays. 58 days = 8 weeks (56 days) + 2 days. Starting Monday, day1 Mon. After 56 days (8 weeks), day56? Since day1 Mon, day7 Sun? Actually day1 Mon, day2 Tue,...,day7 Sun, day8 Mon,... So day56: since 56 mod7=0, day56 is Sunday? Let's see: day1 Mon, day7 Sun, day14 Sun? Actually day7 = Sun, day14 = Sun, day21 = Sun,... so days multiple of 7 are Sundays? Starting Mon, day1 Mon, day2 Tue, day3 Wed, day4 Thu, day5 Fri, day6 Sat, day7 Sun. So day7 = Sun, so day14 = Sun, etc. So day56 = 8*7 = 56, day56 = Sun. Then we have 2 more days: day57 = Mon, day58 = Tue. So the extra days are Mon and Tue. So in 8 weeks, each week has 2 weekend days (Sat and Sun). So weekends in 8 weeks = 8*2=16. Plus extra days: day57 Mon (weekday), day58 Tue (weekday), no extra weekend. So total weekends =16. Total weekdays = 58-16=42. Alternatively, 8 weeks give 40 weekdays (5 per week) plus 2 extra weekdays =42. So Q3: 42.

