11. How many business days (Mon-Fri) from Sunday, June 18, 1995 to Sunday, September 3, 1995 inclusive. Range: Jun 18 to Sep 3. Compute days. Jun 18: Jun start 152, Jun 18 = 152+17=169. Sep 3: Sep start 244, Sep 3 = 244+2=246. Inclusive = 246-169+1=78 days. Day-of-week: Jun 18: day169, (169-1)=168 mod7=0, so Sunday. Sep 3: day246, (246-1)=245 mod7=0, so Sunday. So start Sun, end Sun. Total 78 days. 78/7=11 weeks +1 day? Actually 7*11=77, remainder 1. So 11 weeks and 1 extra day. Starting Sunday, day1 Sun. After 77 days (11 weeks), day77? Since day7 Sat? Let's compute: day1 Sun, day2 Mon, ..., day7 Sat, day8 Sun, ... So day7 = Sat, day14 = Sat, ... day77 = 11*7=77, day77 =? Since 77 mod7=0, day77 = Sat? Actually day7 = Sat, so day14 = Sat, day21 = Sat,... so day77 = Sat. Then extra day: day78 = Sun. So extra day is Sunday (weekend). In 11 weeks, weekends = 11*2=22. Plus extra Sunday =1, total weekends=23. Weekdays = 78-23=55. Alternatively, 11 weeks give 55 weekdays, plus extra day Sunday =0, so total 55. So Q11: 55.

12. Count occurrences of Sunday from Friday, March 17 to Thursday, August 31, 1995 inclusive. Range: Mar 17 to Aug 31. Compute days. Mar 17: Mar start 60, Mar 17 = 60+16=76. Aug 31: Aug start 213, Aug 31 = 213+30=243. Inclusive = 243-76+1=168 days. Day-of-week: Mar 17 day76, (76-1)=75 mod7=5? 7*10=70, remainder5, so Friday? Since 75-70=5, Friday (5). So start Fri. Aug 31 day243, (243-1)=242 mod7=7*34=238, remainder4 => Thursday? 242-238=4, so Thursday. So start Fri, end Thu. Need count of Sundays. First Sunday after start? Start Fri (5), Sunday is 0, difference (0-5) mod7 = 2, so first Sunday on day? day1 Fri, day2 Sat, day3 Sun, so day3. So Sundays on days 3,10,... up to day168. Number = floor((N - r)/7) +1? r = (w-d0) mod7 = (0-5) mod7 = 2. So count = 1 + floor((N-1 - r)/7) = 1 + floor((167-2)/7)=1+floor(165/7)=1+23=24 (since 7*23=161, 165-161=4, floor=23). Actually 165/7=23.571, floor=23, so count=24. Check: Total days 168, full weeks = 24 weeks since 168/7=24 exactly. Since start Fri, end Thu, 24 weeks from Fri to Thu inclusive? That would be exactly 168 days, and each week has one Sunday, so 24 Sundays. So count=24. So Q12: 24.

13. Count occurrences of Thursday from Wednesday, March 22 to Tuesday, April 4, 1995 inclusive. Range: Mar 22 to Apr 4. Compute days. Mar 22: Mar start 60, Mar 22 = 60+21=81. Apr 4: Apr start 91, Apr 4 = 91+3=94. Inclusive = 94-81+1=14 days. Day-of-week: Mar 22 day81, (81-1)=80 mod7= 7*11=77, remainder3 => Wednesday? 80-77=3, so Wednesday. Apr 4 day94, (94-1)=93 mod7=7*13=91, remainder2 => Tuesday? 93-91=2, so Tuesday. So start Wed, end Tue. 14 days = exactly 2 weeks. In 2 weeks from Wed to Tue, there are two Thursdays? Let's list: week1: Wed, Thu, Fri, Sat, Sun, Mon, Tue; week2: Wed, Thu, Fri, Sat, Sun, Mon, Tue. So Thursdays: day2 and day9? Actually day1 Wed, day2 Thu, day3 Fri,... day8 Wed, day9 Thu. So two Thursdays. So answer 2. Q13: 2.

14. How many business days (Mon-Fri) from Tuesday, August 29, 1995 to Thursday, August 31, 1995 inclusive. Range: Aug 29 to Aug 31. Compute days: Aug 29,30,31 = 3 days. Day-of-week: Aug 29: Aug start 213, Aug 29 = 213+28=241. (241-1)=240 mod7=2? 7*34=238, remainder2, so Tuesday (2). Aug 31: Aug 31=213+30=243, (243-1)=242 mod7=4? 242-238=4, so Thursday. So days: Tue, Wed, Thu. All are weekdays. So business days = 3. So Q14: 3.

15. How many business days from Wednesday, July 26, 1995 to Sunday, August 13, 1995 inclusive. Range: Jul 26 to Aug 13. Compute days: Jul 26: Jul start 182, Jul 26=182+25=207. Aug 13: Aug start 213, Aug 13=213+12=225. Inclusive = 225-207+1=19 days. Day-of-week: Jul 26 day207, (207-1)=206 mod7=7*29=203, remainder3 => Wednesday? 206-203=3, so Wed. Aug 13 day225, (225-1)=224 mod7=0, so Sunday. Start Wed, end Sun. 19 days. 19/7=2 weeks (14 days) +5 days. Starting Wed, day1 Wed. After 14 days (2 weeks), day14? Since day7 Tue, day14 Tue? Actually day1 Wed, day7 Tue, day14 Tue. So day14 = Tue. Then extra 5 days: day15 Wed, day16 Thu, day17 Fri, day18 Sat, day19 Sun. So extra: Wed, Thu, Fri, Sat, Sun. Weekends: Sat, Sun (2). In 2 weeks, weekends = 2*2=4. Total weekends = 4+2=6. Weekdays =19-6=13. Alternatively, 2 weeks give 10 weekdays, plus extra Wed, Thu, Fri =3, total 13. So Q15: 13.

16. Between Thursday, March 9, 1995 and Saturday, July 8, 1995 (counting both dates), how many times does Wednesday occur? Range: Mar 9 to Jul 8. Compute days. Mar 9: Mar start 60, Mar 9 =60+8=68. Jul 8: Jul start 182, Jul 8=182+7=189. Inclusive = 189-68+1=122 days. Day-of-week: Mar 9 day68, (68-1)=67 mod7=4? 7*9=63, remainder4, so Thursday? 67-63=4, Thursday. So start Thu. Jul 8 day189, (189-1)=188 mod7=6? 7*26=182, remainder6, so Saturday. So start Thu, end Sat. Need Wednesday count. Wednesday is weekday 3. First Wednesday after start? Start Thu (4), next Wed is day? Difference (3-4) mod7 =6, so first Wednesday on day? day1 Thu, day2 Fri, day3 Sat, day4 Sun, day5 Mon, day6 Tue, day7 Wed. So day7. So first Wed on day7. Then every 7 days. N=122. Number = 1 + floor((N-1 - r)/7) with r = (w-d0) mod7 = (3-4) mod7=6. So count = 1 + floor((121-6)/7)=1+floor(115/7)=1+16=17 (since 7*16=112, 115-112=3, floor=16). So 17 Wednesdays. Alternatively, we can compute full weeks: 122/7=17 weeks remainder 3 days? 7*17=119, remainder 3. Since start Thu, after 119 days (17 weeks), day119? Day1 Thu, day7 Wed? Actually day7 = Wed? Let's check: day1 Thu, day2 Fri, day3 Sat, day4 Sun, day5 Mon, day6 Tue, day7 Wed. So day7 = Wed. So day119 = 17*7 = 119, day119 =? Since pattern: day7,14,..., are Wednesdays. So day119 = 17th Wednesday? Actually day7 is 1st, day14 2nd,... day119 = 17th? Because 7*17=119, so that is the 17th Wednesday if day1 is not Wednesday. Then we have 3 extra days: day120 Thu, day121 Fri, day122 Sat. No extra Wednesday. So total Wednesdays = 17. So Q16: 17.

17. Count weekdays (excl weekends) from Monday, August 7 to Wednesday, August 23, 1995 inclusive. Range: Aug 7 to Aug 23. Compute days: Aug 7 = 213+6=219; Aug 23 = 213+22=235; inclusive=235-219+1=17 days. Day-of-week: Aug 7: day219, (219-1)=218 mod7=1? 7*31=217, remainder1, so Monday (1). Aug 23: day235, (235-1)=234 mod7=3? 7*33=231, remainder3, so Wednesday (3). So start Mon, end Wed. 17 days. Count weekdays: Since start Mon, end Wed, we can count directly. 17 days = 2 weeks (14 days) +3 days. 2 weeks from Mon to Sun? Actually 14 days from Mon to Sun? Let's do: Starting Mon, after 14 days, day14? day1 Mon, day7 Sun, day14? day14 = Sun? Since day7 Sun, day14 Sun. So after 14 days, we have Mon to Sun twice? Actually 14 days inclusive from Mon to Sun? That's 7 days each? Better: In 14 days, there are exactly 2 full weeks, each week has 5 weekdays, so 10 weekdays. Then extra 3 days: day15 Mon, day16 Tue, day17 Wed, all weekdays. So total weekdays = 10+3=13. So Q17: 13.

18. How many business days from Thursday, February 16, 1995 to Wednesday, August 2, 1995 inclusive. Range: Feb 16 to Aug 2. Compute days. Feb 16: Feb start 32, Feb 16=32+15=47. Aug 2: Aug start 213, Aug 2=213+1=214? Actually Aug 2 = 213+1=214 (since Aug 1=213, Aug 2=214). Inclusive = 214-47+1=168 days. Check: Feb 16-28 =13 days (Feb 16-28 inclusive=13? 28-16+1=13), Mar31, Apr30, May31, Jun30, Jul31, Aug1-2=2, total=13+31+30+31+30+31+2=168, yes. Day-of-week: Feb 16 day47, (47-1)=46 mod7=4? 7*6=42, remainder4, so Thursday (4). Aug 2 day214, (214-1)=213 mod7=3? 7*30=210, remainder3, so Wednesday (3). So start Thu, end Wed. 168 days exactly? 168/7=24 weeks. Since start Thu and end Wed, that is exactly 24 full weeks? A week from Thu to Wed inclusive is 7 days, so 24 weeks gives 168 days. So exactly 24 weeks. Each week has 5 weekdays, so business days = 24*5 = 120. So Q18: 120.

19. Count occurrences of Monday from Tuesday, April 18 to Friday, October 27, 1995 inclusive. Range: Apr 18 to Oct 27. Compute days. Apr 18: Apr start 91, Apr 18=91+17=108. Oct 27: Oct start 274, Oct 27=274+26=300. Inclusive = 300-108+1=193 days. Day-of-week: Apr 18 day108, (108-1)=107 mod7=2? 7*15=105, remainder2, so Tuesday (2). Oct 27 day300, (300-1)=299 mod7=5? 7*42=294, remainder5, so Friday (5). So start Tue, end Fri. Need number of Mondays. Monday is 1. First Monday after start? Start Tue (2), next Monday: difference (1-2) mod7 =6, so first Monday on day7? day1 Tue, day2 Wed, day3 Thu, day4 Fri, day5 Sat, day6 Sun, day7 Mon. So day7. Then every 7 days. N=193. Count = 1 + floor((N-1 - r)/7) with r=6. So = 1 + floor((192-6)/7)=1+floor(186/7)=1+26=27 (since 7*26=182, 186-182=4). So 27 Mondays. Alternatively, 193/7=27 weeks remainder 4 days? 7*27=189, remainder 4. Since start Tue, after 189 days, day189? day1 Tue, day7 Mon, so day7 Mon, day14 Mon,... day189? 189/7=27, so day189 is a Monday? Since 27th Monday? Actually day7 is 1st Monday, day14 2nd,..., day7*27=189 is 27th Monday. Then extra 4 days: day190 Tue, day191 Wed, day192 Thu, day193 Fri. No extra Monday, so total Mondays = 27. So Q19: 27.

20. How many Wednesdays from Monday, October 9, 1995 to Thursday, November 9, 1995 inclusive. Range: Oct 9 to Nov 9. Compute days. Oct 9: Oct start 274, Oct 9=274+8=282. Nov 9: Nov start 305, Nov 9=305+8=313. Inclusive=313-282+1=32 days. Day-of-week: Oct 9 day282, (282-1)=281 mod7=1? 7*40=280, remainder1, so Monday. Nov 9 day313, (313-1)=312 mod7=4? 7*44=308, remainder4, so Thursday. Start Mon, end Thu. Need Wednesdays (3). First Wednesday after start? Start Mon (1), Wednesday is 3, difference =2, so first Wednesday on day3? day1 Mon, day2 Tue, day3 Wed. So day3. Then every 7 days. N=32. Count = 1 + floor((31-2)/7)=1+floor(29/7)=1+4=5 (since 7*4=28, 29-28=1). So 5 Wednesdays. Check: days 3,10,17,24,31? 31 ≤ 32? day31 is Wed? Let's check: day31 is? Since day1 Mon, day31 = day1+30, 30 mod7=2, so day31 is Wed? Actually Mon+30 days = Mon+2 mod7 = Wed? Yes. So day31 is Wed, and day32 is Thu, so there are 5 Wednesdays (3,10,17,24,31). So Q20: 5.

21. Between Sunday, April 30, 1995 and Tuesday, October 10, 1995 (counting both dates), what's the total count of business days? Range: Apr 30 to Oct 10. Compute days. Apr 30: Apr start 91, Apr 30=91+29=120? Actually Apr 30 = 91+29? Since Apr 1=91, Apr 30=91+29=120? Wait Apr has 30 days, so Apr 30 is day 91+29=120? Actually 91 is day for Apr1, so Apr2=92,..., Apr30=91+29=120. Yes. Oct 10: Oct start 274, Oct 10=274+9=283. Inclusive